----Distributed environment factor

multiple servers here so few issues which can occur:
-Race Condition
-Synchronization Issue


race condition - 
        simultaneously made req to rate limiter
Client1 ---------------------------------------- Rate Limiter  ---- Counter (Redis DB)
client2 ----------------------------------------             

so there can be race condition when there are overlapping requests.
There are diff strategies to solve this but we see those later


-synchronization issues

we have millions of users and we have multiple servers and multiple rate limiters

c1 - rl1 - s1
c1 - rl2 - s2


same client made call to rl1,2 and s1,2 but s1 and s2 not sync

one solution can be 'sticky sessions' but its not a good solution

another soltion is cenrtalized data store

so multiple clients making req to multiple rate limiters but all rate limiters are attached to single redis store so counters will work fine and can solve this issue

-another issue in distributed env is Performance

if user in US and there are multiple data centers so we need to choose the closest one


